DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260913T170000
UID:260912FtFQ8N-X106W4YdpLHE8mw
DESCRIPTION:This summer\, Music in Place and the City of Sonoma invite you
  to soak up the sunshine\, sip local wine\, and dance to live music at the
  Sonoma Plaza Grinstead Amphitheater during Sonoma Sundays On the Plaza\, 
 a free concert series running June 7 through October 4\, 2026.\n\nEvery Su
 nday from 2:00–5:00 PM\, the Plaza comes alive with an exciting mix of m
 usical styles: blues\, soul\, country\, jazz\, swing\, Americana\, mariach
 i\, and more. With a fresh lineup of acclaimed artists\, there’s somethi
 ng for everyone to enjoy.\n\nSonoma Sundays is all about creating opportun
 ities for the community to come together through the power of live music. 
 Music in Place is excited to bring an incredible range of artists to the P
 laza this summer and continue building connections through music.\n\nSonom
 a Sundays are free and open to all\, thanks to the generous support of the
  Sonoma Community Center\, The Dawn Redwoods Trust\, and the KHR McNeely F
 amily Foundation.\n\nPack your picnic\, bring your dancing shoes\, and mee
 t us on the Plaza!
LOCATION:Grinstead Amphitheater
URL:https://musicinplace.org/event/groove-incident-mitch-woods/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Meditation in the Orchard with Joy Jacobsen at Gold Ridge Organic 
 Farm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260913T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260913T093000
UID:260911t0BtJkD_tEG4vMt6AIcPqA
DESCRIPTION:Start your Sunday with a peaceful introduction to meditation i
 n the tranquil setting of our olive orchard. Led by registered yoga teache
 r\, Joy Jacobsen\, this session offers an opportunity to simply be with yo
 urself\, surrounded by nature\, listening to the gentle vibrations of the 
 world in a safe\, peaceful\, and restorative space.\n\nWe'll begin with a 
 peaceful stroll to the orchard from our Farm Shop. Feel free to bring your
  own mat\, though we'll also provide one if needed. Then we'll move into g
 entle standing stretches and mindful breathing—essential practices that 
 prepare the body to become limber\, relaxed\, and comfortable for stillnes
 s. As you settle into a 20-minute meditation\, Joy will hold space for you
 r practice\, opening and closing the session with the soothing sound of a 
 singing bowl.\n\nWe'll conclude the experience back at the farm shop with 
 fresh apple cider and sliced heirloom apples.\n\nJoy brings firsthand expe
 rience from training in Hatha and Vinyasa yoga in Goa\, India\, and from c
 ompleting a three-week silent meditation retreat in Thailand. Her welcomin
 g\, supportive approach creates an ideal environment for both experienced 
 practitioners and those new to meditation. You'll also find her warmth at 
 Gold Ridge Organic Farms\, where she manages the Farm Shop and is a famili
 ar\, friendly face to our community.
LOCATION:Gold Ridge Organic Farms
URL:https://www.exploretock.com/gold-ridge-organic-farms/event/618530/medi
 tation-in-the-orchard-with-joy-jacobsen
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Winona & The Northern Still (Matinée)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260913T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260913T160000
UID:260909KB_JPwd39UyU4vLTJpRLOg
DESCRIPTION:$18 General Admission\n\nDoors at 4:00pm. \n\nShow from 4:45-7
 :30pm with one intermission\n\nEarlybirds!\n\n$3 off each ticket when you 
 use the code earlybird10 at checkout. Offer ends September 6th.\n\nProm
 o Codes are not applicable at the door.\n\nCodes are not case sensitive
 \, but must be typed as one word.\n\nWinona is a musician\, songwriter\, 
 and performer based in Northern California. Her songs are mythic\, her voc
 als haunting\, full of melancholic longing and timeless beauty. Rooted in 
 the folk music of the 1960s and inspired by modern indie songstresses\, Wi
 nona’s sound is at once nostalgic and dew-fresh unique. Her influences i
 nclude Feist\, Kate Wolf\, Courtney Marie Andrews\, and \\(of course\\) Jo
 ni.\n\nNow backed by an immensely talented band\, Winona’s songs are fre
 e to come entirely alive\, with shimmering chord progressions\, siren-like
  harmonies\, and melodies that will spirit you away to the stars.\n\nIn ad
 dition to her own music\, she can be seen performing as one third of the f
 olk trio Wyld Iris\, singing sweet harmonies in the Laura T Lewis Band\, o
 r collaborating with other musical friends.\n\nhttps://winonadoesmusic.com
 / https://www.instagram.com/winonadoesmusic https://www.youtube.com/@winon
 adoesmusic\n\nDawn Angelosante’s \\(piano\\) voice wraps lyrics into a d
 reamscape of sound and story\, touching on love\, friendship\, heartbreak\
 , and self-reflection. Tony Gibson’s \\(guitar\\) songwriting blends inf
 ectious melodies with honest\, emotionally resonant lyrics. His music feel
 s familiar and fresh. Michael Fecskes \\(cello\\)\, a classically trained 
 cellist and composer\, adds a unique depth to the group’s sound. His com
 positions are rich and soulful. Together\, they form The Northern Still\,
  a dynamic acoustic/folk-pop trio. Since 2021 they’ve combined their ind
 ividual voices and musical influences into a lush\, intimate sound\, with 
 haunting vocal harmonies. Whether performing original compositions or thei
 r fresh takes on covers\, they’ve captivated audiences throughout the No
 rth Bay.\n\nhttps://www.instagram.com/thenorthernstillmusic https://www.y
 outube.com/@wearethenorthernstill https://www.facebook.com/thenorthernsti
 ll Recommended If You Like: Joni Mitchell\, Gillian Welch\, Watchhouse
LOCATION:The Lost Church
URL:https://thelostchurch.my.salesforce-sites.com/ticket#/instances/a0FUh0
 0000Bd8fJMAR
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
