SUMMARY:macbitches
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260913T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260913T153000
UID:260820HsyIw9I2W0aaVykmyobp9g
DESCRIPTION:“macbitches takes Shakespearean themes and grounds them in 
 a recognizable\, modern reality — a smarter\, theater-centered Mean Gir
 ls\, if you will. It’s funny\, sharp\, and unafraid to let women be comp
 licated.” - Jeanette Seisdedos\, director\n\nmacbitches takes a darkly 
 funny look at the toxic\, high-stakes world of university theater\, center
 ing on a freshman who unexpectedly lands the role of Lady Macbeth. The pla
 y centers on freshman acting major Hailey\, who unexpectedly scores the co
 veted role of Lady Macbeth. Her upperclassmen rivals immediately invite he
 r over to “celebrate.” As the Fireball and Svedka flow\, the young wom
 en interrogate their own ambitions as well as the power structures that ha
 ve shaped their education—and when the night spirals into violent and sh
 ocking acts of betrayal\, they come to learn that what’s done cannot be 
 undone.\n\n\\*Content Advisory: Strong profanity\, physical and psycholog
 ical violence\, heavy substance abuse and underage drinking\, discussions 
 of mental illness and sexual misconduct\, and themes of betrayal and suici
 de. Recommended for mature audiences 16+.\n\nWritten by Sophie McIntosh\n\
 nDirected by Jeanette Seisdedos\n\nRunning Time: 90 minutes with no interm
 ission\n\nSeptember 4th\, 5th\, 6th\, \\*10th\, 11th\, 12th\, 13th\, 18th\
 , 19th\, 20th.\n\nFriday and Saturday Shows: 7:30 PM\n\nSunday Matinee: 
 2:00 PM\n\n\\*Value Thursday: 7:30 PM\n\n Adults: $25\n\nStudent w/ID:
  $10\n\n\\*Special Value Thursday Performance:  Pay What You Can\n\nWri
 tten by Sophie McIntosh\n\nDirected by Jeanette Seisdedos
LOCATION:The Raven Performing Arts Theater
URL:https://raventheater.org/events/macbitches/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Meditative Birding California Biodiversity Day 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260913T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260913T110000
UID:260817zJsQyKjcmUyvaqa0YH2NXQ
DESCRIPTION:We will start off by sitting quietly for 10 minutes 
 with Merlin app recording in 3 different locations\, followed by
  about 10 minutes of discussion of the birds we heard\, using 
 Cornell to confirm their calls and songs before moving onto the
  next sitting spot. We will also saunter (while looking for bir
 ds) between the locations for a total distance of ~1.3 mile & 
 ~250’ ascent. Birding by ear lends itself to meditation because
  it works best when you sit silently and listening closely (i.e
 .\, if Merlin *hears* something you did not\, it reminds you th
 at your mind has wandered).\n\nMeet at the White Barn parking lo
 t. Tickets are $10 for general audiences\, $5 for students\, you
 th (12-17 year olds\; must be accompanied by a parent or legal
  guardian)\, Sugarlof members\, Sugarloaf or RFO volunteers\, and
  free for children under 12. **Tickets day-of on site are $15 
 and might not be available**. \n\nEnsure you install the Merlin 
 app on your device along with the bird pack for US: West Coast
  before you arrive for the hike\, as there is no cell service
  is non-existent in the areas we'll be meandering. Wear layers 
 (it's likely to be cold in the early morning) and sturdy shoes.
  Bring binoculars\, at least a quart of water\, sun protection\,
  a bird-identification guide (if you have one)\, and if desired\
 , a snack. If you are willing to carry a portable chair for a
 bout 1.3 miles\, you are welcome to bring it\, but there will 
 be benches at all of our stops. Parking fees apply.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/meditative-birding-ca-biodiversity-day-2026-913
 2026
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
