BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Watercolor | Building Technique II\, with Nancy Ballard
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260915T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260915T120000
UID:260912k8GnWjYxB0CYnWkHEIhmww
DESCRIPTION:Building on the skills and confidence you developed in the fir
 st class\, this watercolor workshop invites you to take your ideas a step 
 further. Explore how a simple sketch\, thoughtful composition\, and expres
 sive use of color can transform an idea into a finished painting.\n\nWe'll
  work larger and bolder while exploring watercolor techniques including:\n
 \nWet-on-wet paintingLoose interpretation and expressive mark-makingCreati
 ng shadows and depthEnhancing backgroundsWorking in black and whiteExplori
 ng the many variations and possibilities of mixing greens\n\nBring a favor
 ite photograph\, a live flower or small plant\, or even a meaningful memor
 y to use as inspiration. No matter where you are in your artistic journey\
 , you'll be encouraged to experiment\, have fun\, and focus on the larger 
 picture rather than striving for perfection. There are no mistakes in art&
 mdash\;only opportunities to explore.\n\nPlease Note: There will be a $10 
 supply fee paid directly to the Nancy on the day of the class.\n\nNancy's 
 classes sell out quickly and we only 16 spots available\, so reserve your 
 spot now!\n\n If you've taken Nancy's Gentle Watercolor workshop\, this cl
 ass will build on the skills and techniques you've already developed. If y
 ou're new to the series\, you'll find a welcoming\, supportive environment
  where you can jump right in. All experience levels are welcome\, and you'
 ll be guided along the way.\n\nNancy Ballard's love of art began in childh
 ood\, when she first discovered the magic of brush and paint&mdash\;a sens
 e of wonder that continues to shape her work today. After a full life as a
  mother\, grandmother\, and corporate professional\, she returned to art f
 ollowing her retirement in 2006\, studying watercolor with Mary L. Harden 
 at Strybing Arboretum. In 2009\, she was recognized as a Master Artist of 
 Botanical Illustration by the San Francisco Botanical Garden Society. Nanc
 y has also worked as a gallery curator and exhibiting artist throughout th
 e Bay Area\, sharing her botanical work in galleries\, wineries\, hospital
 s\, and nonprofit spaces while supporting environmental awareness through 
 art.\n\nLearn More: \n\nwww.nancyballard.com\n\nArtwork by Nancy Ballard
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/watercolor-doodletangle-wi
 th-nancy-ballard-2?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
