BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Night at Great Company
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260917T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260917T183000
UID:260912PP19ZmafcUGFuIG4xiFyhA
DESCRIPTION:Join Great Company on Thursday\, September 17th for Art Night
  at 5:30pm. Art night is a free\, non-ticketed event\, with suggested don
 ations for supplies.\n\nArt Night is a monthly gathering focused on commu
 nity\, creativity\, and connection.\n\nMonthly Creative Gathering: A play
 ful\, low-pressure space to create alongside friends and community.\n\nPro
 ject: We feature 1 new guided art project each month with a short intro a
 nd demo to get you started. We always have a library of art supplies avail
 able if you’re not feeling the guided project.\n\nFlexible Supplies: Us
 e the materials we provide for a $5–$10 donation\\*\, or bring your own
  project to work on for free. \\(\\*This is all self-funded\, so we appre
 ciate any help.\\)\n\nAll Skill Levels: No experience needed! Our roaming
  hosts are there to offer ideas\, tips\, and encouragement—it’s about 
 the process\, not perfection.
LOCATION:Great Company
URL:https://montgomeryvillageca.com/event/art-night-at-great-company/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jueves Sediento – Live Música Regional Mexicana  Select a date 
 and
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260917T220000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260918T013000
UID:260911ycIUvmNTHUGhUHDny4gPZg
DESCRIPTION:Free live música regional mexicana every Thursday at 10 PM! D
 anny Waralu\, beer bucket specials\, dancing\, free popcorn & no cover. 21
 +\n\nThursday nights are getting louder at Barrel Proof Lounge . Jueves Se
 diento brings live música regional mexicana to Downtown Santa Rosa with D
 anny Waralu \, serving up a night inspired by sierreño\, rancheras\, corr
 idos\, regional favorites\, and more . It's the perfect soundtrack for col
 d beer\, good company\, and a packed dance floor.\n\nThe music starts at 1
 0 PM \, making Jueves Sediento the place to keep the night going. Stop in 
 after dinner\, meet up with friends\, or make Barrel Proof your last stop 
 of the evening.\n\nEvery Thursday  Live Music • 10:00 PM Always FREE  
 No Cover  21+  Free Popcorn\n\nThursday Night Specials  Beer Bucket Spe
 cials  Rotating drink promotions throughout the night\n\nMusic\, dancing\
 , cold drinks\, and a room full of people ready to have a good time. That'
 s what Thursday nights are all about.\n\nBarrel Proof Lounge 501 Mendocino
  Ave. Downtown Santa Rosa\n\nCheck out **www.BarrelProofLounge.com** for u
 pcoming live music\, comedy\, karaoke\, trivia\, and special events!\n\nJu
 eves Sediento – Live Música Regional Mexicana\n\nLos jueves por la noch
 e tienen nuevo destino en Barrel Proof Lounge .\n\nJueves Sediento present
 a a Danny Waralu con una noche de música regional mexicana en vivo \, ins
 pirada en el sierreño\, las rancheras\, los corridos y muchos de los esti
 los que ponen a todos a cantar y bailar.\n\nLa música comienza a las 10:0
 0 PM \, el momento perfecto para seguir la noche con amigos\, disfrutar un
 as cervezas bien frías y llenar la pista de baile.\n\nTodos los Jueves  
 Música en Vivo • 10:00 PM ¡Siempre GRATIS!  Sin cover  Solo para may
 ores de 21 años  Palomitas gratis\n\nEspeciales de los Jueves\n\n Espec
 iales en cubetas de cerveza  Promociones en bebidas durante toda la noche
 \n\nBuena música\, buena compañía y un gran ambiente te esperan todos l
 os jueves en el centro de Santa Rosa.\n\nBarrel Proof Lounge 501 Mendocino
  Ave. Downtown Santa Rosa\n\nVisita **www.BarrelProofLounge.com** para con
 ocer nuestros próximos conciertos\, comedia\, karaoke\, trivia y eventos 
 especiales.
LOCATION:Barrel Proof Lounge
URL:https://JuevesSediento.eventbrite.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Culinary Student Lunch Pop-UP
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260917T113000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260917T130000
UID:260911xOKq8BgU406A6pzZjWCIhA
DESCRIPTION:Our Culinary Student Pop-Up Lunch Cafe is back! There will be 
 two lunch service windows: Wednesday through Friday on September 16th-18t
 h and again 23rd-25th\, 11:30 AM to 1 PM. This tradition marks the culmina
 tion of our current adult culinary job training cohort in Petaluma\, with 
 every dish on the menu inspired and shaped by the students themselves. It'
 s a chance for our trainees to put their new skills to the test working th
 e line in a real service setting - and for you to taste what they've been 
 working on and cheer them on as they graduate into their next chapter.\n\n
 Consider treating your whole team or company to lunch those weeks - it's a
  great way to support our students while feeding your crew! There’s limi
 ted space to eat onsite\, so please plan to pick up\, take it with you\, a
 nd enjoy.\n\nHead to sonomafamilymeal.org for the full menu and option t
 o place your order online in advance.
LOCATION:Sonoma Family Meal Community Kitchen
URL:http://sonomafamilymeal.org
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mikayla McVey
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260917T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260917T180000
UID:260910lLiYgStV0UmyYERrKndW1Q
DESCRIPTION:Mikayla McVey writes & performs from the beating\, blistered\,
  blissed out heart of the West. Born in Virginia and raised up in the holy
  golden Northern California hills\, McVey has come to understand music as 
 a major thread that ties together community and an opportunity to practice
  magic in one of its most accessible & transmittable forms. Music has alwa
 ys been home and she genuinely hopes / time turns everything / into song.\
 n\nShe currently resides in Oakland\, California\, and has made homes in r
 ural South America\, Los Angeles\, Las Vegas\, and the 35ft cavern of a 19
 86 International School bus named Splendor.
LOCATION:Little Saint
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/1039941865?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=2
 87&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pints with Politicians: Brianna Rogers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260917T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260917T193000
UID:260909rPh5yqX_60WFjoe74Gaqtg
DESCRIPTION:We're putting the public house back into the pub! Meet and sha
 re a drink with your local\, District 4 Councilmember Candidates!\n\nWe of
 fered up—to all the candidates for City Council District 4—an opportun
 ity to come hang for a night at our Coal Shed Brewery and meet and greet w
 ith voters. And they all said yes! Each candidate gets their own night: 6p
 m\, one candidate\, no moderator\, casual\, and for sure … all welcome. 
 Come have a conversation \\(and grab a pint\\) with your council candidate
 !\n\nEach District 4 candidate is posting up at our Coal Shed Brewery for 
 a casual meet and greet with voters. No stage\, no moderator\, just a chan
 ce to have a conversation \\(and grab a pint\\) with your council candidat
 e! \n\n‍09/17 – Brianna Rogers\, 10/01 – Chris Platzer\, 10/08 – 
 Charles Palmares\n\n‍We're not endorsing anyone\, but we have mad respec
 t for anyone who is willing to step into the arena. Let's keep the communi
 ty and conversation flowing.
LOCATION:Coal Shed Brewery
URL:https://www.mareislandbrewingco.com/events/pints-with-politicians-bria
 nna-rogers-vallejo-district-4
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ross Barbieri\, Y8S\, Christina Lovett
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260917T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260917T223000
UID:260909d8CB50FU8kyOIwXo0gSv4w
DESCRIPTION:$15 General Admission\n\nDoors at 7:30pm.\n\nShow from 8:15-10
 :30pm with one intermission\n\nEarlybirds!\n\n$3 off each ticket when you 
 use the code earlybird11 at checkout. Offer ends September 13th.\n\nPro
 mo Codes are not applicable at the door.\n\nCodes are not case sensitiv
 e\, but must be typed as one word.\n\nRooted in Sonoma County\, singer-son
 gwriter Ross Barbieri crafts a modern\, genre-bending evolution of Ameri
 cana. His music balances warm\, inviting vocals with intricate\, dynamical
 ly woven guitar lines. Drawing inspiration from artists like Foy Vance\, M
 adison Cunningham\, and The Barr Brothers\, Barbieri’s songwriting leave
 s space for the listener—painting an unfinished picture where personal e
 xperiences fill in the gaps. He is currently in the studio recording his d
 ebut EP. @rossmakesnoise\n\nY8S is Bay Area musician Isaac Yates. Raised 
 in a musical family and sharpened behind the kit in local bands\, he write
 s from a wide well of influences — Mali blues\, ’90s grunge\, West Coa
 st underground hip-hop — and blends them into something hard to pin down
 : heavy-hitting live drums\, soulful vocals\, and fine-tuned pop productio
 n. New music monthly.\n\nhttps://www.isaacy8s.com\n\nhttps://youtube.com/@
