BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Marin Farmers Markets
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260917T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260917T130000
UID:260909esZr9w5dK0-Hshsl9P0eJw
DESCRIPTION:Price: Free\n\nSponsor: Marin Center\n\nExplore the bounty of 
 summer at the Marin Farmers Markets. Taste vine-ripened tomatoes\, corn th
 at was picked that morning\, and peaches so juicy you have to bend over ju
 st to get a bite. Farm-fresh eggs\, grass-fed beef\, artisan c heeses\, ra
 w milk\, and freshly baked breads complete the shopping exper ience. Speci
 alty prepared foods and handmade art add to the magic of the market.\n\nEn
 joy the intimate feeling of the Thursday Marin Farmers Market\, an ideal p
 lace to meet for lunch and pick up fresh produce for the weekend. Discover
  the abundance and diversity of product at the celebrated Sunday Marin Far
 mers Market\, the third largest farmers market in California. Turn your do
 llar into a vote for local sustainable agriculture\, shrink your eco-footp
 rint\, and revive the feeling of being intimate ly connected to your food 
 by meeting your farmers face-to-face. The market takes place rain or shine
 .\n\nwww.aginstitutemarin.org
LOCATION:Marin Veterans' Memorial Auditorium
URL:https://www.marincounty.gov/county-marin-calendar
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Gain Speaking Confidence with Mare Island Toastmasters
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260917T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260917T203000
UID:260903pR_4Z5vQL0-zrpdrOWVzwQ
DESCRIPTION:We meet in-person only on the 1st and 2nd Thursdays of the mon
 th. However\, you can catch us online every Thursday unless the meeting da
 te falls on a holiday.\n\nPlease register at https://signup.com/go/WiniixA
 \n\nWhat is Toastmasters About?\n\nUsually at our meetings\, we will have 
 a prepared speech\, and a speech evaluation. The Grammarian and Wizard of 
 Ah's will listen for turns of phrases and the use of filler words. We also
  practice impromptu speaking during the section of the meeting called Tabl
 e Topics. During Table Topics\, at a recent meeting\, we were asked what w
 e felt was the biggest communication problem or challenge. What would you 
 answer in a fast moment? Table topics will challenge you to think quickly 
 and give an answer without preparation.\n\nYou will also hear tips on publ
 ic speaking skills at our upcoming meeting. Whether you're a seasoned trav
 eler or just looking for some adventure from the comfort of your home\, th
 is event is perfect for you.\n\nToastmasters International is all about co
 mmunication excellence\, and for 100 years and counting\, Toastmasters hav
 e been expressing themselves better\, practicing\, and evaluating in a fun
  club environment\, shining all around the world.\n\nTo find out more--Msg
  us on our webpage \\(under Contact Us\\) button at\n\nhttps://mareisland.
 toastmastersclubs.org/\n\nIf you will join us in-person on the first or se
 cond Thursday of the month\, we meet this week at Kaiser Hospital Bldg. A.
  3rd floor meeting room. When you enter the hospital building\, go past th
 e piano to the elevator. Go to the 3rd floor. Exit left out of the elevato
 r and left at the hall. Go past the gym and take a left at the hall. Walk 
 down the long hall to the meeting room.
URL:https://signup.com/go/WiniixA
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Golden Hour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260917T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260917T170000
UID:2609033lKNB1ESVE2BaIFRZSJPbQ
DESCRIPTION:This September and October\, Lucci Lambrusco is taking over 
 Golden Hour at El Dorado Kitchen\, bringing a taste of Italian aperitivo
  culture to the patio all season long.\n\nSettle in for a late afternoon o
 f Lucci Lambrusco\, Italian wines\, cocktails and shareable bites made for
  lingering. Throughout the two-month takeover\, Lucci will be joined every
  Thursday by a rotating lineup of guest wineries\, importers and producers
 \, each stopping by to pour something special and share a little more abou
 t what’s in your glass.\n\nThe season kicks off on Thursday\, September
  3\, with live music\, Lucci Lambrusco\, passed pizzas and arancini on the
  patio.\n\nLUCCI ITALIAN GOLDEN HOUR TAKEOVER Monday–Friday | 3:00–
 5:00 PM September & October\n\nTHURSDAY GUEST WINE SERIES Every Thursday |
  3:00–5:00 PM\n\nSeptember 3 | Lucci Lambrusco\n\nSeptember 10 | Oliver 
 McCrum Wines\n\nSeptember 17 | Mora Estate\n\nSeptember 24 | Idlewild Wine
 s\n\nOctober 1 | Cline Family Cellars\n\nOctober 8 | Unti Vineyards\n\nOct
 ober 15 | Massican\n\n...and more to come!\n\nLucci is pouring all season 
 long\, with a few friends joining along the way.\n\nCome for a glass. Stay
  for another.\n\nJOIN US FOR GOLDEN HOUR
LOCATION:El Dorado Hotel
URL:https://eldoradosonoma.com/el-dorado-kitchen/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
