SUMMARY:Introduction to Reduction Linocut
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260919T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260919T130000
UID:2608235jTR4hH4eESMKAiPnoXXgg
DESCRIPTION:Saturdays Weekly · 4 Weeks\n\nDate & Time\n\nSeptember 5 – 
 26\, 2026\n\n10:00 AM – 1:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 208\n\nCategory\n\nP
 rintmaking\n\nExperience Level\n\nBeginning\n\nAges\n\n18 and older\n\nReg
 istration Cost:\n\n$195\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\n$30\n\nTotal Registration Cos
 t:\n\n$225\n\nIn this special four-week workshop\, participants will explo
 re the unique art of reduction relief printmaking. Acclaimed guest artist\
 , Tomoko Murakami\, will demonstrate how to create multi-color prints from
  a single linoleum block. The main idea is to gradually carve away parts o
 f the block and print each new layer of color\, with each layer building o
 n the previous one. The course covers the entire process\, from designing 
 and planning\, to carving techniques\, inking\, registration\, and printin
 g with both hand and printing press methods. Participants will learn to ex
 plore the possibilities of color mixing and layering\, enabling students t
 o achieve intricate designs and a wide range of visual effects. You will g
 ain an understanding of the materials\, processes\, and innovations involv
 ed in this unique form of relief print printing!All levels are welcome\, i
 ncluding continuing linocut students. Please note: This class requires ha
 nd dexterity to maneuver the carving tool. Participants should feel comfor
 table standing\, and using tools with sharp blades and edges.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/introduction-to-reduction-l
 inocut/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Redwood Writers General Meeting Genre Panel
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260919T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260919T133000
UID:260822lWpy8iIYt0G4Z53oRVR-pA
DESCRIPTION:Want to learn inside tips about writing and meet local authors
 ?\n\nYou're invited to\n\nRedwood Writers General Meeting\, networking\, a
 nd potluck \\(Please bring a dish to share of you like.\\)\n\nJoin us for 
 an engaging panel conversation with three fiction writers\, each a master 
 of their own genre — Crime/Thriller\, Speculative Fiction\, and Romance.
  From the thrill of the unexpected to the pull of unforgettable characters
 \, our panelists will pull back the curtain on what it really takes to cra
 ft a novel readers can’t put down.\n\nWhether you’re a lifelong bookwo
 rm\, an aspiring writer\, or simply curious about what goes on behind the 
 page\, this is your chance to hear firsthand how great stories are made\, 
 and why genre matters more than you might think. This meeting is for all s
 torytellers\, no matter what genre you write in!\n\nPanelists:\n\nEllen Ki
 rschman Crime/Thriller\n\nPlease welcome Ellen Kirschman\, author of the f
 ive-book Dot Meyerhoff mystery series. A retired police psychologist herse
 lf\, Ellen brings real insider knowledge to her fictional counterpart Dot 
 — a police psychologist who takes orders from no one and keeps solving c
 rimes she should be leaving to the cops. Ellen lives in Santa Rosa and is 
 a member of Mystery Writers of America\, Sisters in Crime\, and the Public
  Safety Writers Association. https://ellenkirschman.com/\n\nMara Lynn John
 stone Science Fiction & Fantasy\n\nPlease welcome Mara Lynn Johnstone\, au
 thor of multiple books exploring other worlds — aliens\, robots\, shapes
 hifters\, magicians\, and the occasional precisely-timed witty banter. Kno
 wn for memorable characters and a knack for turning genre tropes on their 
 head\, Mara Lynn is also President of Redwood Writers. You can find her up
  a tree\, in a bookstore\, or lost in thought… https://www.maralynnjohns
 tone.com/\n\nCrissi Langwell Small-Town Romance & Women’s Fiction\n\nPle
 ase welcome Crissi Langwell\, a multi-genre author whose work spans romanc
 e\, women’s fiction\, and speculative storytelling — all centered on d
 eeply human characters and heartfelt emotional journeys. From her award-wi
 nning Sunset Bay series to her newest small-town Lahoma Springs romances\,
  her novels blend heartache\, hope\, and humor into stories that feel both
  intimate and real. Crissi lives in Northern California with her writerly 
 husband\, their Maine Coon cat Cleo\, and a chair of laundry that really n
 eeds to get its act together. https://crissilangwell.com/
LOCATION:Finley
URL:https://redwoodwriters.org/sept-2026-genre-panel/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Crepe Paper Flowers: Dandelions
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260919T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260919T143000
UID:2608228pOVTplGL0O98grw9NmuhA
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, September 19\, 2026 10:00 am to 2:30 pm\n\nLocation
 \n\nRoom 201\, Fiber Arts Studio\n\nCategory\n\nFiber Arts\n\nExperience L
 evel\n\nBeginning\n\nAges\n\n18 and older\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$75\n\n
 Materials Fee:\n\n$5\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$80\n\nDon’t think o
 f dandelions only as weeds—discover the beauty of these often-overlooked
  wildflowers! Join us to create charming crepe paper dandelions and their 
 distinctive leaves in this beginner-friendly workshop. You’ll learn tech
 niques for cutting\, shaping\, and assembling the intricate petals and fol
 iage that capture the character of these familiar blooms. No prior experie
 nce is needed. Participants will leave with some finished crepe paper dand
 elion stems and the skills to continue making more at home. All materials 
 provided. Please bring a bag lunch or snacks and a beverage/water bottle.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/crepe-paper-flowers-dandeli
 ons/
