DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260919T130000
UID:260803oSpSgi1ijUGYwjwNJ02udw
DESCRIPTION:Fridays Weekly · 8 Weeks\n\nDate & Time\n\nAugust 7 – Septe
 mber 25\, 2026\n\n10:00 AM – 1:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 117\, Ceramics 
 Studio\n\nCategory\n\nCeramics\, Extended Classes\n\nExperience Level\n\nA
 ll Levels\n\nAges\n\n17\\+\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$295\n\nExplore paperc
 lay\, handbuilding\, and multi-firing techniques to create small-to-medium
  sculptures – methods adaptable to any scale or artistic style.\n\nprogr
 am overview\n\nStudents will work with a variety of techniques and materia
 ls\, including paperclay\, nontraditional approaches to handbuilding\, and
  constructing sculptures over multiple firings. The class will focus on sm
 all to medium sculptural work\, but these techniques are applicable to any
  scale and genre.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/intuitive-construction-in-c
 lay/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
