BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Melba's Kitchen Big Band - Jazz Super Sunday
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260920T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260920T160700
UID:260820ljlzqgNh8UuIs1yuMc-ysA
DESCRIPTION:MELBA’S KITCHEN Big Band - the “crackling 14\\+ piece all-
 woman unit…” \\(Downbeat magazine\\) - presents a concert and dance to
  celebrate the music of Black women musical geniuses Melba Liston\, Mary L
 ou Williams\, and their friends. 2026 is Melba Liston’s Centennial\, and
  the band is raring to return to Vallejo and bring the party! Over nearly 
 ten years of performing at venues including YOSHI’S Oakland\, SFJAZZ Min
 er Auditorium\, Berkeley’s Freight and Salvage\, the Healdsburg Jazz Fes
 tival\, SF’s de Young Museum\, the band has excited audiences and earned
  rave reviews. “They’re so astonishing…They’re so swinging!”- De
 e Spencer\, jazz professor. “A marvelous night with good vibes all aroun
 d!” - Rebecca Mauleon\, SFJAZZ. “A talent-packed ensemble…” - Andy
  Gilbert\, jazz journalist. Sunday afternoon’s lawn party is your chance
  to tear up the outdoor dance floor AND soak in the strains of authentic b
 lues-drenched jazz compositions from the thirties through today - tunes as
  new as tomorrow morning. MELBA’S KITCHEN will be playing Quincy Jones\,
  Stevie Wonder\, Sly Stone\, Basie\, Abbey Lincoln\, and more\, including 
 sophisticated and swinging Liston\, Mary Lou Williams\, and band originals
 . Just the ticket for a hip and relaxing step into Bay Area Autumn! A litt
 le background about Melba and Mary Lou: The jazz great MELBA LISTON made f
 ormidable contributions to jazz. Liston toured with and wrote for Dizzy Gi
 llespie\, Quincy Jones\, Gerald Wilson\, and collaborated for decades - in
  the Ellington/ Strayhorn mode - with piano titan Randy Weston. Liston had
  a great big beautiful sound on the trombone\, and was a pioneer as a woma
 n in jazz. She arranged for many\, including Abbey Lincoln\, Betty Carter\
 , Marvin Gaye\, Clark Terry\, and Ruth Brown. MARY LOU WILLIAMS\, an activ
 ist for jazz\, was a virtuosic and inspired pianist\, composer\, and arran
 ger. Although Williams attained a level of visibility and recording succes
 s\, her work has remained in relative shadow. MELBA’S KITCHEN intends to
  bring Liston’s and Williams’ names into your musical household. Melba
  Liston has earned her spot in the jazz firmament with other 2026 jazz cen
 tennial greats\, like Coltrane\, Miles and Randy Weston. Come dance and ce
 lebrate the music with us! Food: TBD Misc: Gate opens at noon. Minors welc
 ome\, kids 12 and under are free. Well mannered/managed puppy dogs are wel
 come in the outside venue area. We will have seating for everyone.  Your o
 wn comfy folding chairs are welcome.  \\*You may bring your own water and 
 "light snacks." \\*\\*NO large catering trays\, chafing dishes\, tables\, 
 or other large party supplies allowed. Must coordinate celebrations with v
 enue. info@vinogodfather.com NO outside alcohol of any kind! TICKETS ARE $
 22 Advance TICKETS ARE $27 Day of Show
LOCATION:Vino Godfather Winery
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/981514994924906/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
