BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Peace in the Plaza
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260921T113000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260921T173000
UID:260830cgCpzTGqRkeaPZ9_6naKWQ
DESCRIPTION:Peace in the Plaza is a public event inspired by the United Na
 tions International Day of Peace and presented by Sonoma Ashram. This free
  half-day event will include live music\, ongoing yoga classes\, a wellnes
 s hub\, children’s activities\, and community tabling. The event will be
  presented in partnership with local civic\, faith\, and wellness leaders.
  Musicians will include Sukhawat Ali Khan Band\, Vox Populi\, Sophia Sanch
 ez\, and René Jenkins.\n\nAs part of the opening ceremony\, there will be
  a minute of silence at 12 PM to coincide with the UN International Day of
  Peace moment of silence around the world. Guided meditations and an after
 noon talk will be provided by Sonoma Ashram Founder Baba Harihar Ramji\, a
 ffectionately known as “Babaji." Babaji has inspired people in the Sonom
 a Valley for over 35 years. His teachings emphasize living simply\, inner 
 freedom\, and selfless service.\n\nThe intention is to inspire our communi
 ty to remember the inner peace within us all—because true peace begins a
 t home and expands naturally to our families\, neighborhoods\, and the wor
 ld.
LOCATION:Sonoma Plaza
URL:https://sonomapeaceintheplaza.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Keith Hansen: "For the Love of Birds and the Joy of Birding"
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260921T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260921T203000
UID:260823hGd8l5SM9ESjDwPvuPWqQQ
DESCRIPTION:Join Keith Hansen for a lively dive into what inspired him to 
 take up illustrating birds and eventually to become a bird book author. He
  has recently finished his 13th and 14th books entitled Hansen’s Field G
 uide to the Birds of the Sierra Nevada and The Birds of Point Reyes.\n\nTa
 lk begins at 7pm\, following 6:30pm Madrone Audubon monthly general meetin
 g.\n\nKeith\, who comes from an artistic family\, has been looking at bird
 s from the age of 10 and illustrating them since the 12th grade. Growing u
 p\, he and his older brother Rob birded every spare moment they could\, fi
 rst in the woods of Maryland\, before moving to Fresno\, California in 197
 0. He did work at Point Reyes Bird Observatory’s Palomarin Field Station
  and then spent 9 years on the SE Farallon Island\, where he banded\, phot
 ographed and studied hundreds of birds up close. He has traveled extensive
 ly through the New World Tropics including Mexico\, Guatemala\, Costa Rica
 \, Panama\, Ecuador\, Colombia\, Trinidad and Tobago\, Guyana\, the Amazon
 \, and the Galapagos\, where he filmed 100s of species for his artwork. Hi
 s current project is illustrating all the birds of N. America for an app c
 alled FLOCK.\n\nCome and join us!
LOCATION:First United Methodist Church
URL:https://www.madroneaudubon.org/speakers
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
