BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:California Native Creations Art Show
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260921T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260921T163000
UID:260909d_biYhPSBk6nrrQupyo_bw
DESCRIPTION:September is the 17th Annual Pomo Honoring Month. On Monday\, 
 Sept. 14\, the 6th California Native Creations Art Show opens Person Senio
 r Wing\, Finley Community Center\, 2060 W. College Ave.\, Santa Rosa\, CA.
  The show is free and open to the public Monday – Friday\, 8:30 a.m.-4:3
 0 p.m.\, through November 19.\n\nThe established and up-and-coming native 
 artists create with digital media\, paint and traditional materials in the
 ir art\, weaving\, regalia\, beadwork\, jewelry\, baskets and quilts. The
  artists include:\n\n·         Meyo Marrufo\, painter\, guest cur
 ator for the de Young Museum and the Sonoma Valley Art Museum\,\n\n·  
        Buffie Campbell\, Vice Chair\, Sherwood Valley Rancheria\, cu
 ltural teacher and master basket maker\,\n\n·         Henry Edwar
 d Frank\, Yurok/Kashaya Pomo\, who will show paintings and work with Legos
  titled Mind Prison\,\n\n·         Digital artist Nicolas \\(Nico
 \\) Vargas\, Kashia Band of Pomo Indians\, whose art was featured at the 5
 5th Annual Stanford Powwow.\n\n·         plus Gloria Carretero\; 
 Rose Hammock\; Rudy Hammock\; Jocelyn Garcia\; Arella Ortega LaRose\, Kash
 ia Band of Pomo Indians\; Angelica Smith\, Manchester Point Arena and Yoka
 yo Rancheria\; Maria Pasalo\; Michelle Napoli\; Martina Morgan\, Kashia Ba
 nd of Pomo Indians\; Hands Lopez\; Shashoni Hanover-Redenbaugh\; Katie Wi
 lliams-Elliott\, Juan Partida\, and Mia Pasalo\, Big Valley Pomo Tribe.
LOCATION:Person Senior Wing\, Finley Community Center
URL:http://www.pomoproject.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Formative Influence Art Exhibit
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260921T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260921T160000
UID:260909KArTGUTDuE22dZIO4watEQ
DESCRIPTION:Formative Influence explores the transformative power of light
  across five bodies of work. Inspired by the landscapes of Northern Califo
 rnia and the American West\, the exhibition examines the shift from photog
 raphy\, where light is observed and captured\, to painting\, where light i
 s created to shape new visual experiences. Rather than documenting the lan
 dscape\, these works evoke its emotional resonance\, emphasizing atmospher
 e\, memory\, and perception over literal representation.
LOCATION:Marin Center
URL:https://www.marincultural.org/exhibitions
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Golden Hour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260921T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260921T170000
UID:260903dq3nyFcUlEOOPwjTpKDwYg
DESCRIPTION:This September and October\, Lucci Lambrusco is taking over 
 Golden Hour at El Dorado Kitchen\, bringing a taste of Italian aperitivo
  culture to the patio all season long.\n\nSettle in for a late afternoon o
 f Lucci Lambrusco\, Italian wines\, cocktails and shareable bites made for
  lingering. Throughout the two-month takeover\, Lucci will be joined every
  Thursday by a rotating lineup of guest wineries\, importers and producers
 \, each stopping by to pour something special and share a little more abou
 t what’s in your glass.\n\nThe season kicks off on Thursday\, September
  3\, with live music\, Lucci Lambrusco\, passed pizzas and arancini on the
  patio.\n\nLUCCI ITALIAN GOLDEN HOUR TAKEOVER Monday–Friday | 3:00–
 5:00 PM September & October\n\nTHURSDAY GUEST WINE SERIES Every Thursday |
  3:00–5:00 PM\n\nSeptember 3 | Lucci Lambrusco\n\nSeptember 10 | Oliver 
 McCrum Wines\n\nSeptember 17 | Mora Estate\n\nSeptember 24 | Idlewild Wine
 s\n\nOctober 1 | Cline Family Cellars\n\nOctober 8 | Unti Vineyards\n\nOct
 ober 15 | Massican\n\n...and more to come!\n\nLucci is pouring all season 
 long\, with a few friends joining along the way.\n\nCome for a glass. Stay
  for another.\n\nJOIN US FOR GOLDEN HOUR
LOCATION:El Dorado Hotel
URL:https://eldoradosonoma.com/el-dorado-kitchen/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Haunted Wine Tour & Tasting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260921T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260921T173000
UID:260831SNJA0NShO0SSQ3e8ta8WlQ
DESCRIPTION:This fall\, Buena Vista Winery invites you to uncover the myst
 eries\, legends\, and ghostly encounters woven into more than 165 years of
  history. Led by Sonoma historian and actor George Webber\, this immersive
  90 minute experience journeys through the historic Press House and Champa
 gne Cellars\, revealing true tales of unexplained happenings reported by B
 uena Vista team members and visitors throughout the years.\n\nHear the sto
 ries of the Glowing Ghostly Shirt\, the Little Girl Who Says Hi\, the myst
 erious Ghost Party on the Second Floor\, the Old Man Who Walked Into a Sto
 ne Wall\, and other strange occurrences that continue to add to the legend
  of Buena Vista.\n\nAlong the way\, explore some of the winery’s most in
 triguing spaces\, including the Bubble Lounge\, Cave of Curiosities\, and 
 Wine Tool Museum\, while enjoying five Buena Vista wines tasted throughout
  the experience\, including a taste drawn directly from barrel.\n\nAnd\, a
 s with any journey through Buena Vista’s extraordinary past\, you never 
 quite know when the winery’s legendary founder\, Count Agoston Haraszthy
 \, may choose to make an appearance.\n\nHistory\, wine\, mystery\, and per
 haps a spirit or two await.
LOCATION:Buena Vista Historical Winery
URL:https://eventvesta.com/events/160340/t/tickets
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
