BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Apple U-Pick at Gold Ridge Organic Farms
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T113000
UID:260911YWF1en1pV0KUoGbme-LoKA
DESCRIPTION:**Our popular Apple U-Pick Experiences return for a second yea
 r!**\n\nExperience the magic of harvest season at Gold Ridge Organic Farms
 \, where you can hand-select the most flavorful Honeycrisp or Fuji apples 
 straight from our certified organic orchard.\n\nTimed entries from 8:30am.
  Last orchard entry at 11:30am.\n\nAdmission: $8 for adults\, $3 for child
 ren. Registration required.\n\nU-Pick apples: $4 per pound.\n\n**Apple U-P
 ick FAQs** \n\nDo I need a reservation? \n\nYes! Please reserve your tim
 e slot on our reservation site. Reservations help us ensure everyone has a
  wonderful experience without overcrowding.  \n\nCan I show up without a
  reservation? \n\nWe require reservations to maintain our capacity limit
 s and ensure everyone enjoys their visit to the fullest.  \n\nCan I canc
 el my reservation?  \n\nAbsolutely! You can cancel your reservation up 
 to 48 hours before your scheduled time by calling us at 707-823-3100. Plea
 se note that cancellations made less than 48 hours in advance will result 
 in forfeiture of the entrance fee. \n\nCan I bring my dog?  \n\nDogs a
 re not permitted in the orchard\, with the exception of service animals. T
 his policy helps ensure the safety and comfort of all our visitors. \n\nC
 an I bring a stroller into the orchard?  \n\nFor safety reasons\, strol
 lers aren't allowed in the orchard\, but you're welcome to leave yours at 
 the check-in area where it will be safe and waiting for you!  \n\nI requ
 ire mobility accommodations. Can I still pick apples in the orchard?  \n
 \nYes. Please call us on 707-823-3110 once you’re made a reservation and
  we can provide suitable transportation into our orchard.\n\nWhy is there 
 an entrance fee?  \n\nThe entrance fee helps us maintain our beautiful 
 orchard and keep our experienced staff on hand to ensure everyone has a sa
 fe and enjoyable experience. \n\nHow much are the apples?  \n\nOur del
 icious U-pick apples are $4.00 per pound.  \n\nWhat variety of apples wi
 ll we be harvesting?  \n\nYou'll be picking either Honeycrisp or Fuji a
 pples (depending on seasonal availability).  \n\nCan I harvest heirloom 
 apples?  \n\nWhile heirloom apples aren't available for U-pick\, we off
 er many wonderful heirloom varieties for purchase in our Farm Shop.  \n\
 nAre your apples organic?  \n\nYes\, all our apples are organically gro
 wn and certified annually by Oregon Tilth!
LOCATION:Gold Ridge Organic Farms
URL:https://goldridgeorganicfarms.ticketspice.com/u-pick
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:DAVID NELSON BAND RIDES AGAIN Campout 5
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T100000
UID:260910lOfup1U_7ECTHFmv3tZFXQ
DESCRIPTION:September 26 & 27\, 20261 & 2 Day Camping Event\n\nHermitage M
 usic presents:\n\nDAVID NELSON BAND RIDES AGAIN Campout 5\n\n             
                                                                           
                                                                           
                                                                           
                                                                           
                                                                           
                         \n\n\n\n \n\nWelcome to the 5th Annual David Nelso
 n Band Rides Again Weekend. Make sure to get your tickets purchased early\
 , as tickets are going fast. We will be sending traveling directions to al
 l Ticket Holders. Please purchase tickets before the event and preferably 
 not at the door.\n\nA joyous Summer gathering of music! This uplifting exp
 erience leaves everyone feeling grateful for being in attendance. Lots of 
 space to roam freely with friends. Views in all directions. Hiking trails\
 , Swimming for the kids at the Pool with adults present. Kids are free 12 
 yrs. and under. Arts & Crafts for kids. Lots of Craft Vendors. \n\nService
  Dogs are accepted as long as they are accredited. In the past dogs were f
 ree to come\, but owners let them roam freely. No campfires or cooking. \n
 \nThere will be Food provided for Breakfast\, Lunch & Dinner\, & Breakfast
  Latte Bar choices in the tasting room\, all for purchase. Free Spring Wat
 er. \\(please bring your water bottles\\).  Beverages\, Beer\, Wine\, & So
 ft Drinks all for purchase in the Tasting Room\,  2 Free Wine Tasting tick
 ets per day.\n\nAll are welcome: friends\, family & kids\, to spend 1 or 2
  amazing days of camping or come for the day\, Sat. or Sun.  RVs come set 
 up early on Fri 9/25 at 3:00 to 7pm. Gates open on Sat. & Sun. 9/26 & 9/27
  at 10:00 am. Load out your campsite by noon on Monday. \n\nCAMPING AT THE
  EVENT Bring shade items\, sunscreen\, misquito spray. We will have mister
 s and shade\, plus you can chill in the Star Stage Barnand tasting room an
 d still see the main stage. Best to stay out of the direct sun for long pe
 riods of time. \n\nBring: flashlights & camping gear\, hiking boots\, swim
 suits & beach towels\, low back chairs\, We have warm summer nights with c
 ool breezes from the coast in the afternoon\,bring warm clothes for night 
 time temps\, just in case it gets cold this time of year.\n\n We have 2 Ho
 t Water Star Showers and dressing rooms. The Indoor Star Stage in the main
  indoor center of the barn & green room for Musicians to chill.There will 
 be bands playing in between acts on the The Corral Stage & The Star Stage\
 , while the Main Galaxy Stage is getting geared up for the next bands. See
  the Line up posted around. Our wine & olive oil are for purchase & visit 
 our merch table in the tasting room. \n\nThere is Camping available for al
 l. The Fox Grove: Tent & Auto Camping\, The Oak Grove: RV Parking only. Pl
 ease bring RVs in Friday from 3 -7pm. Electric hook up fee is included in 
 ticket price. Bucks Corral: Tent camping only no vehicles aloud\, plus VIP
  Tent Camping. Eagle Camp:Extreme wilderness camping with 4WD only. Hikers
  can hike to Eagles Camp for more awesome views!\n\nTo become a Volunteer 
 or to be a Merch Vendor contact hermitagemusicmgmt@proton.me\n\nHOTELS BOO
 K FAST \n\nIf you prefer not to camp\, there are other accommodations avai
 lable in Cloverdale\, Geyserville\, Healdsburg\, Hopland\, Boonville & Uki
 ah.\n\nTICKETS must be purchased before these EVENTS and then you will rec
 eive directions to the Events through an email from CalTix.com before the 
 Event. Cloverdale is 15 mins. from the event.\n\nCLOVERDALE: SUPER 8: Call
  707- 893-7057 - Furber Ranch Plaza. Address: 1147 S Cloverdale Blvd\, Clo
 verdale\, CA 95425. Only 15 minutes from venue.\n\nCLOVERDALE WINE COUNTRY
  INN & SUITES: Call 707-894-7500 Address: 324 S Cloverdale Blvd\, Cloverda
 le\, CA 95425. Only 15 minutes from venue.\n\nGEYSERVILLE INN: Call 707- 8
 57-4343 Address: 21714 Geyserville Ave\, Geyserville\, CA 95441 Only 20 mi
 nutes from venue. \n\nGEYSERVILLE: ISIS OASIS: Call 707-857-4747 Thurs. th
 ru Sun. 2 to 8 pm or call Director di Traci at 619-632-2064. Pet Friendly:
 Dogs are welcome on approval/$10. Must take dogs with you. CABERNET COTTAG
 E is really cute for a couple or family. Grateful Dead recorded Terrapin h
 ere. Jerry Garcia's favorite place to chill.Address: 20889 Geyserville Ave
 \, Geyserville\, CA 95441. Only 20 minutes from venue.\n\nHEALDSBURG: BEST
  WESTERN: Call \\(707\\) 433-0300 Address: 198 Dry Creek Rd\, Healdsburg\,
  CA 95448 Pet Friendly\n\nHOPLAND: THACTHER HOTEL: Call  888-461-2017   Ho
 tel Address: 13401 US-101\, Hopland\, CA 95449  Only 15 mins from venue.HO
 PLAND: STOCKFARM INN: Call 707-744-1977  Hotel Address:  13441 US-101\, Ho
 pland\, CA 95449  Only 15 mins from venue.\n\nHotels in Ukiah for better r
 ates. Only 35 minutes from Ukiah via Hopland and Mpontain House Road..\n\n
 Tickets on Sale Now: Tell your friends!
LOCATION:LE VIN WINERY aka Seawolf Wines
URL:https://www.caltix.com/e/davidnelson5?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
