BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wine\, Women and Dementia
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T124500
UID:260909JsuKQy6EU06Aj6zzCP5ZDQ
DESCRIPTION:“Wine\, Women\, & Dementia” is a powerful and uplifting do
 cumentary that will be showcased on Saturday\, September 26\, from 10:00 a
 m -12:45 pm at the Carol Ellis Auditorium at the Santa Rosa Junior College
  Campus\, 680 Sonoma Mountain Parkway\, Petaluma.\n\n The film follows a
  caregiver’s journey across the country\, gathering stories from others 
 navigating dementia care. It captures the beauty and brutality of dementia
  caregiving\, balancing the heartbreaking with the humorous.\n\n Followi
 ng the film\, there will be a panel discussion that includes the filmmaker
 . In addition\, information from local resources will be available.  \n\
 n Please plan to arrive 30–45 minutes early to visit our community reso
 urce tables\, meet representatives from local organizations\, and discover
  services and support available for caregivers and families before the pro
 gram begins.\n\nThis event is sponsored by The Village Network of Petaluma
 \, a nonprofit organization that advocates for innovative community-based
  solutions to improve quality of life and expand choices at all stages of 
 aging.\n\n The event is free of charge\; however\, registration is requir
 ed.  To attend\, contact The Village Network at 707.776.6055
LOCATION:Carol Ellis Auditorium\, Santa Rosa Junior College
URL:https://villagenetworkofpetaluma.org
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Healdsburg Internation Short Film Festival 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T223000
UID:2609096EZvypwV20Wp5Z8aAPMfhQ
DESCRIPTION:This three-day festival runs from September 25th through Sept
 ember 27th. Organized in collaboration with the **Healdsburg Center for t
 he Arts (HCA**)\, HISFF 2026 coincides with HCA’s **Festival of the Art
 s**\, creating a vibrant\, art-filled weekend.\n\nHISFF 2026 kicks off wi
 th an Opening Night Soirée\, a lively red-carpet arrival and photo op at
  the Raven\, and an exquisite collection of mixed genre short films. Festi
 vities continue with multiple screening sessions\, a Saturday night party 
 at **The Rooftop at the Harmon Guest House**\, and a filmmaker breakfast\
 , culminating in an awards ceremony on Sunday night.\n\nOur panel of notab
 le judges from the entertainment industry makes the HISFF an attraction fo
 r new and veteran filmmakers alike — people like **Ed Begley\, Jr.\, Lar
 aine Newman\, Billy Ray\, Tom Waits**\, and so many more. Several judges a
 re attending the festival this year\, including writer Billy Ray (*The Hun
 ger Games* and the soon-to-be released *The Hunger Games: Sunrise On the
  Reaping* )\, who will make a book-signing appearance at the Raven on Sat
 urday\, September 26th (Time TBD).\n\nVisit our booth at the Healdsburg F
 estival of the Arts on Saturday\, September 26th\, from 10 am to 6 pm on 
 Center Street in front of HCA (just steps away from the Raven). The street
  will be lined with booths featuring fine arts\, crafts\, jewelry\, poetry
 \, live music\, food trucks\, and more!\n\nCopperfield’s is organizing a
  free-admission book-signing event with screenwriter (and festival jurist)
  Billy Ray at the Raven from 11:00 am\, also on Saturday\, September 26th.
  Books will be available for purchase and signing\, but it’s best to ord
 er your copy ahead of time from Copperfield’s.\n\n**All Access Pass: $17
 5. Includes:**\n\n\\- Red-Carpet arrival and photo op begins at 6 pm at th
 e Raven.\n\n\\- Opening Night Kick-Off Screening Block\, 7:00 pm.\n\n\\- O
 pening Night Kick-Off Soirée\, 8:30 pm at Portalupi Wines.\n\n\\- Saturda
 y Night Sweet & Uncorked Social at the beautiful Harmon House Rooftop\, 8:
 15 pm.\n\n\\- Every screening session\, including the filmmaker Q&A sessio
 ns.
LOCATION:The Raven Performing Arts Theater
URL:https://raventheater.org/events/hisff2026/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
