BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Help Save Newts: Call for Volunteers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T120000
UID:260822TZlHFeAlvUmI_vFTqdn_zA
DESCRIPTION:Volunteers Needed to Save Newts\n\nThe Chileno Valley Newt Bri
 gade is gearing up to rescue the thousands of newts\, frogs and other crea
 tures as they migrate across a dangerous road. Can you help?\n\nThe traini
 ng will be held on Sept. 26th on Chileno Valley Road in Petaluma.\n\nWhat:
  Wearing a reflective vest\, you’ll use a flashlight and bucket to carry
  animals across the road. You’ll also keep count using iNaturalist\, col
 lecting data that reveals population trends.\n\nWhen:  You'll join a team
  that goes out once a week between mid-October and mid-March.\n\nRegistrat
 ion required: go to www.chilenovalleynewtbrigade.org and fill out the volu
 nteer form.
LOCATION:Chileno Valley Newt Brigade
URL:http://www.chilenovalleynewtbrigade.org
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Country Line Dancing Night ft. Dustin Saylor & The Stowaways
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T190000
UID:260822DnpFWbAaiU-mZy-Yr5Dcaw
DESCRIPTION:**Date:** Saturday\, September 26\, 2026\n\n**Time:** Doors 6
  PM | Lessons 7-8 PM | Live music throughout the night\n\n**Tickets:** $20
  Advance | $25 Door | Coyote Sonoma Members Receive $5 Off\n\nJoin us for 
 line dancing lessons from Grapevine Dance! Plus live music from Dustin Say
 lor & The Stowaways.\n\nAbout Dustin Saylor:\n\nDustin Saylor\, a Northern
  California-born country singer-songwriter\, has made a name for himself a
 s the #1 Country/Folk artist in the San Francisco Bay Area. His musical jo
 urney began in childhood\, first at the piano and later as a guitarist and
  singer for his high school youth group and local church. Despite early ch
 allenges\, including a devastating American Idol rejection in 2009\, Saylo
 r had a transformative moment on his long drive home\, realizing that true
  success required full commitment. Embracing his calling\, he quit bartend
 ing\, pursued a music degree at Sonoma State University\, and became a ful
 l-time musician. Over the years\, he has performed alongside artists like 
 Tyler Rich\, Chase Rice\, and Daughtry\, with his sound often compared to 
 Thomas Rhett and Chris Stapleton. His songwriting is deeply personal\, sha
 ped by his early experiences of adoption and the contrasting struggles and
  joys of his life. Through his music\, Saylor seeks to inspire\, heal\, an
 d create a space where people can connect beyond labels. Committed to his 
 craft\, he remains "all in\," determined to sing and play music for the re
 st of his life.
LOCATION:Coyote Sonoma
URL:https://shop.coyotesonoma.com/country-line-dancing-with-dustin-saylor-
 -the-stowaways-926-p255.aspx
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Culture in Choreography - Asian American Pioneers In Dance
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T180000
UID:2608225ozHnPa7XE2YxBtAPVFHyw
DESCRIPTION:*Culture In Choreography*\, a new ongoing cinematic series at 
 The Jarvis Conservatory\, explores diverse perspectives and experiences in
  dance.\n\nThe inaugural screening features two documentaries by acclaimed
  filmmaker Jennifer Lin (*Beethoven in Berlin*)\, offering complementary p
 erspectives on the Asian American experience in ballet. Together\, the fil
 ms journey from a study of the past to a benchmark for the future\, celebr
 ating Asian American pioneers in dance and the artists who are carrying th
 eir legacy forward.\n\nThrough these compelling stories\, *Culture In Cho
 reography* invites audiences to reflect on the people\, histories\, and c
 ultural perspectives that continue to shape the world of dance.\n\n**TEN T
 IMES BETTER** unveils the remarkable story of an 88-year-old Chinese black
 jack dealer in Las Vegas whose forgotten past reveals an extraordinary pla
 ce in ballet history.\n\n**ABOUT FACE: DISRUPTING BALLET** is a 60-minute 
 documentary following two New York City dancers as they challenge the elit
 e ballet world to confront and eliminate racial stereotypes embedded in be
 loved classics such as *The Nutcracker* and *La Bayadère*.\n\nTogether\, 
 the films serve as bookends to the story of Asians in ballet—one uncover
 ing a hidden chapter from the past\, the other documenting artists shaping
  a more inclusive future. Both films were directed by acclaimed filmmaker\
 , Jennifer Lin (Beethoven In Beijing).\n\nSaturday\, September 26th 4:00pm
  Tickets are $15
LOCATION:Jarvis Conservatory
URL:https://jarvisconservatory.ticketspice.com/ten-times-better-and-about-
 face
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
