BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:DAVID NELSON BAND RIDES AGAIN Campout 5
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260927T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260927T100000
UID:2609108wFC0u1Jm0eFNPV_MC6iLA
DESCRIPTION:September 26 & 27\, 20261 & 2 Day Camping Event\n\nHermitage M
 usic presents:\n\nDAVID NELSON BAND RIDES AGAIN Campout 5\n\n             
                                                                           
                                                                           
                                                                           
                                                                           
                                                                           
                         \n\n\n\n \n\nWelcome to the 5th Annual David Nelso
 n Band Rides Again Weekend. Make sure to get your tickets purchased early\
 , as tickets are going fast. We will be sending traveling directions to al
 l Ticket Holders. Please purchase tickets before the event and preferably 
 not at the door.\n\nA joyous Summer gathering of music! This uplifting exp
 erience leaves everyone feeling grateful for being in attendance. Lots of 
 space to roam freely with friends. Views in all directions. Hiking trails\
 , Swimming for the kids at the Pool with adults present. Kids are free 12 
 yrs. and under. Arts & Crafts for kids. Lots of Craft Vendors. \n\nService
  Dogs are accepted as long as they are accredited. In the past dogs were f
 ree to come\, but owners let them roam freely. No campfires or cooking. \n
 \nThere will be Food provided for Breakfast\, Lunch & Dinner\, & Breakfast
  Latte Bar choices in the tasting room\, all for purchase. Free Spring Wat
 er. \\(please bring your water bottles\\).  Beverages\, Beer\, Wine\, & So
 ft Drinks all for purchase in the Tasting Room\,  2 Free Wine Tasting tick
 ets per day.\n\nAll are welcome: friends\, family & kids\, to spend 1 or 2
  amazing days of camping or come for the day\, Sat. or Sun.  RVs come set 
 up early on Fri 9/25 at 3:00 to 7pm. Gates open on Sat. & Sun. 9/26 & 9/27
  at 10:00 am. Load out your campsite by noon on Monday. \n\nCAMPING AT THE
  EVENT Bring shade items\, sunscreen\, misquito spray. We will have mister
 s and shade\, plus you can chill in the Star Stage Barnand tasting room an
 d still see the main stage. Best to stay out of the direct sun for long pe
 riods of time. \n\nBring: flashlights & camping gear\, hiking boots\, swim
 suits & beach towels\, low back chairs\, We have warm summer nights with c
 ool breezes from the coast in the afternoon\,bring warm clothes for night 
 time temps\, just in case it gets cold this time of year.\n\n We have 2 Ho
 t Water Star Showers and dressing rooms. The Indoor Star Stage in the main
  indoor center of the barn & green room for Musicians to chill.There will 
 be bands playing in between acts on the The Corral Stage & The Star Stage\
 , while the Main Galaxy Stage is getting geared up for the next bands. See
  the Line up posted around. Our wine & olive oil are for purchase & visit 
 our merch table in the tasting room. \n\nThere is Camping available for al
 l. The Fox Grove: Tent & Auto Camping\, The Oak Grove: RV Parking only. Pl
 ease bring RVs in Friday from 3 -7pm. Electric hook up fee is included in 
 ticket price. Bucks Corral: Tent camping only no vehicles aloud\, plus VIP
  Tent Camping. Eagle Camp:Extreme wilderness camping with 4WD only. Hikers
  can hike to Eagles Camp for more awesome views!\n\nTo become a Volunteer 
 or to be a Merch Vendor contact hermitagemusicmgmt@proton.me\n\nHOTELS BOO
 K FAST \n\nIf you prefer not to camp\, there are other accommodations avai
 lable in Cloverdale\, Geyserville\, Healdsburg\, Hopland\, Boonville & Uki
 ah.\n\nTICKETS must be purchased before these EVENTS and then you will rec
 eive directions to the Events through an email from CalTix.com before the 
 Event. Cloverdale is 15 mins. from the event.\n\nCLOVERDALE: SUPER 8: Call
  707- 893-7057 - Furber Ranch Plaza. Address: 1147 S Cloverdale Blvd\, Clo
 verdale\, CA 95425. Only 15 minutes from venue.\n\nCLOVERDALE WINE COUNTRY
  INN & SUITES: Call 707-894-7500 Address: 324 S Cloverdale Blvd\, Cloverda
 le\, CA 95425. Only 15 minutes from venue.\n\nGEYSERVILLE INN: Call 707- 8
 57-4343 Address: 21714 Geyserville Ave\, Geyserville\, CA 95441 Only 20 mi
 nutes from venue. \n\nGEYSERVILLE: ISIS OASIS: Call 707-857-4747 Thurs. th
 ru Sun. 2 to 8 pm or call Director di Traci at 619-632-2064. Pet Friendly:
 Dogs are welcome on approval/$10. Must take dogs with you. CABERNET COTTAG
 E is really cute for a couple or family. Grateful Dead recorded Terrapin h
 ere. Jerry Garcia's favorite place to chill.Address: 20889 Geyserville Ave
 \, Geyserville\, CA 95441. Only 20 minutes from venue.\n\nHEALDSBURG: BEST
  WESTERN: Call \\(707\\) 433-0300 Address: 198 Dry Creek Rd\, Healdsburg\,
  CA 95448 Pet Friendly\n\nHOPLAND: THACTHER HOTEL: Call  888-461-2017   Ho
 tel Address: 13401 US-101\, Hopland\, CA 95449  Only 15 mins from venue.HO
 PLAND: STOCKFARM INN: Call 707-744-1977  Hotel Address:  13441 US-101\, Ho
 pland\, CA 95449  Only 15 mins from venue.\n\nHotels in Ukiah for better r
 ates. Only 35 minutes from Ukiah via Hopland and Mpontain House Road..\n\n
 Tickets on Sale Now: Tell your friends!
LOCATION:LE VIN WINERY aka Seawolf Wines
URL:https://www.caltix.com/e/davidnelson5?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tosca by Giacomo Puccini
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260927T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260927T190000
UID:260909d3AK8CgX406W37EznhEmXA
DESCRIPTION:Free Admission. Become a member to support Verismo Opera's new
  free admission policy.  Membership for $30 per person will be good for a
  year from purchase and will entitle members to early seating \\(before no
 n-members\\) for performances.\n\n Stage Director: Eliza O’ Malley \n\
 nConductor: Carlos Hernandez\n\nWith Chamber Orchestra and English Supert
 itles \n\nIn association with Mira Theatre Guild\n\nFor company informati
 on and to purchase memberships visit www.verismoopera.org\n\nLove\, lust\
 , jealousy\, deception\, torture\, murder\, suicide – all in one opera 
 – Tosca.  An idealistic artist\, a celebrated singer and a corrupt poli
 ce chief engage in a fierce battle of wills in this tempestuous tale of cr
 uelty and deception. With its themes of political intrigue\, sexual intimi
 dation and official hypocrisy\, Puccini’s great masterpiece rings true t
 oday through its powerfully dramatic and gorgeous music.\n\nMira Theatre G
 uild\, 51 Daniels Avenue\, Vallejo\, CA 94590\n\n- September 12\, 2026 \\(
 Saturday 7:00pm\\)\n\n- September 13           \\(Sunday 3:00pm\
 \)\n\n- September 19           \\(Saturday 7:00pm\\)\n\n- Septem
 ber 20           \\(Sunday 3:00pm\\)\n\n- September 26     
       \\(Saturday 7:00pm\\)\n\n- September 27           \\
 (Sunday 3:00pm\\)
LOCATION:Mira Theatre Guild
URL:http://www.verismoopera.org
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Healdsburg Internation Short Film Festival 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260927T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260927T223000
UID:260909ZNwsZgnj-E2w7XXrvliskQ
DESCRIPTION:This three-day festival runs from September 25th through Sept
 ember 27th. Organized in collaboration with the **Healdsburg Center for t
 he Arts (HCA**)\, HISFF 2026 coincides with HCA’s **Festival of the Art
 s**\, creating a vibrant\, art-filled weekend.\n\nHISFF 2026 kicks off wi
 th an Opening Night Soirée\, a lively red-carpet arrival and photo op at
  the Raven\, and an exquisite collection of mixed genre short films. Festi
 vities continue with multiple screening sessions\, a Saturday night party 
 at **The Rooftop at the Harmon Guest House**\, and a filmmaker breakfast\
 , culminating in an awards ceremony on Sunday night.\n\nOur panel of notab
 le judges from the entertainment industry makes the HISFF an attraction fo
 r new and veteran filmmakers alike — people like **Ed Begley\, Jr.\, Lar
 aine Newman\, Billy Ray\, Tom Waits**\, and so many more. Several judges a
 re attending the festival this year\, including writer Billy Ray (*The Hun
 ger Games* and the soon-to-be released *The Hunger Games: Sunrise On the
  Reaping* )\, who will make a book-signing appearance at the Raven on Sat
 urday\, September 26th (Time TBD).\n\nVisit our booth at the Healdsburg F
 estival of the Arts on Saturday\, September 26th\, from 10 am to 6 pm on 
 Center Street in front of HCA (just steps away from the Raven). The street
  will be lined with booths featuring fine arts\, crafts\, jewelry\, poetry
 \, live music\, food trucks\, and more!\n\nCopperfield’s is organizing a
  free-admission book-signing event with screenwriter (and festival jurist)
  Billy Ray at the Raven from 11:00 am\, also on Saturday\, September 26th.
  Books will be available for purchase and signing\, but it’s best to ord
 er your copy ahead of time from Copperfield’s.\n\n**All Access Pass: $17
 5. Includes:**\n\n\\- Red-Carpet arrival and photo op begins at 6 pm at th
 e Raven.\n\n\\- Opening Night Kick-Off Screening Block\, 7:00 pm.\n\n\\- O
 pening Night Kick-Off Soirée\, 8:30 pm at Portalupi Wines.\n\n\\- Saturda
 y Night Sweet & Uncorked Social at the beautiful Harmon House Rooftop\, 8:
 15 pm.\n\n\\- Every screening session\, including the filmmaker Q&A sessio
 ns.
LOCATION:The Raven Performing Arts Theater
URL:https://raventheater.org/events/hisff2026/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:No Cell Sundays: Marcus & Devin
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260927T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260927T143000
UID:260909S2RsYaSzNU-fx80otDeH5w
DESCRIPTION:**Soul Meets Keys: Marcus & Devin Live**\n\nJoin us for No Cel
 l Sundays with Marcus & Devin\, a duo that transforms Sunday afternoons in
 to something extraordinary.\n\nMarcus Urani is one of Northern California'
 s most celebrated pianists and keyboardists. Educated in musical theory an
 d an original member of Groundation\, Marcus has toured the world and spen
 t 25+ years composing\, arranging\, producing\, and playing with countless
  musical acts. With mastery across nearly all genres\, Marcus creates rich
  musical landscapes that captivate from the first note.\n\nPaired with voc
 alist and lyricist Devin Ruddick's emotive and soaring vocals\, this duo d
 elivers a one-two punch that captivates without intrusion—adding melodic
  bliss as they cover a catalog of meaningful artists spanning seven decade
 s.\n\n**What's No Cell Sundays?**\n\nIt's simple: disconnect from your dev
 ices\, reconnect with great wine\, live music\, and the people around you.
  *Check your phone with us at the door and receive a complimentary tasting
 .* Bring a blanket\, grab a glass\, and spend your Sunday the way it was m
 eant to be spent.
LOCATION:Hook & Ladder Winery
URL:https://www.hookandladderwinery.com/event/no-cell-sundays-marcus-devin
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Reggae Roadhouse!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260927T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260927T180000
UID:2609081H2iR_rVukOmH8EIQBuTrQ
DESCRIPTION:If you are a lover of all styles of Reggae music\, then this i
 s the event for you! Come enjoy a sound system session hosted by the Uncon
 ditional Love Sound DJs and dance to tunes ranging from ‘60s Ska to mode
 rn Steppers! Get ready for 6-hours of heavy rhythms exploring the many sub
 genres of Reggae music (Rock Steady\, Roots\, Dancehall\, Dub\, Lovers Roc
